    35	| R1 | **S0002 AC4 says "an authorization denial → `403`".** No engine route returns 403 for a denial. Every denial is the non-disclosing 404 (`brain-api.yaml` `Forbidden`: "user denials are reported as 404"; master blueprint section 118.2). | The design keeps the engine unchanged. 403 is used only for `csrf_rejected`, and a denial stays the existing 404 with the session kept (never 401). The AC4 proof shows each outcome is distinct and the session survives a denial. **Proposed PM wording correction at feature G0:** "an authorization denial → the engine's existing non-disclosing `404`, with the session kept". Confirmed by the operator with `approve-phase-b` (2026-11-27). |
    36	| R2 | **S0008 AC2 says "no credential verification runs"**, but AC4 requires a valid credential from a throttled client to be served, which needs verification. | Verification stays local while throttled: cached JWKS, session lookup, no JWKS refetch, no IdP call. A rejected credential then gets 429 with no event row. AC2 is proven as "no per-request `authentication_event`, no upstream IdP call". **Proposed PM wording correction at feature G0.** Confirmed by the operator with `approve-phase-b` (2026-11-27). |
    37	| R3 | S0005 AC7 depends on authentik's end-session behavior. | The provider's invalidation flow becomes `default-invalidation-flow` (ADR-0082 D2). The end-session URL carries `client_id` and `post_logout_redirect_uri`, with no `id_token_hint`. The signed-out page's "Sign in" sends `prompt=login`. Feature G0 verifies both against authentik 2026.2 before S0005 is built. |
    38	| R4 | S0006 AC1 needs tenant and knowledge-base display names; `tenant` and `knowledge_base` have no name column. | Migration 0018 adds nullable `display_name` (expand-only). Null names show a localized "Unnamed knowledge base" with a short ID suffix. Dev seed data sets names. |
    39	| R5 | `/reviews/{id}` is both an engine path and the natural shell route. | One public origin: the shell at `/`, the engine under `/api/`, with the prefix stripped by the front. The OpenAPI paths stay at the root (SOLUTION-PATTERNS section 3: no `/api` prefix in the contract). The shell route is `/reviews/:reviewItemId`. |
    40	| R6 | ADR-0051 says "tenant switch". | Implemented as the active knowledge-base selector (Phase A reconciliation 3). A change of tenant is a change of selected membership. |
    41	| R7 | BLUEPRINT section 2.1 still calls the session transport "proposed direction (ADR-0051, open)" and leaves the frontend test stack to Phase B. | Updated in this run: ADR-0051 decision recorded, ADR-0082 runtime, stack confirmed (ADR-0082 D12). |
